2026-09-07 13:24:46 | WARNING  | app.graph.nodes:review_text:118 - Tweet review rejected generated tweet | iteration=1 | feedback=The phrase "productive friction" is a meaningful concept but the surrounding language feels over-polished and formulaic in a way that signals AI-generated writing. Specifically, "flourishes through productive friction," "safe consensus," "bold, distilled work," and "where talent serves the project, not just the ego" read like a stack of buzzword phrases rather than natural professional prose. It also leans a bit abstract and could be made more concrete with a brief example or sharper take. Consider tightening the language so it sounds like something a real person would type, not a string of clever-sounding fragments.
